## 2. Tooling & Config Files

### [package.json](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/package.json)

This is the "ingredients list" for your project. Key sections:

| Section | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `scripts` | Commands you can run: `npm run dev` starts the dev server |
| `dependencies` | Libraries your app **needs to run** (React, Axios, Framer Motion…) |
| `devDependencies` | Tools needed only **during development** (Vite, Tailwind…) |

**Key dependencies explained:**

| Library | What it does |
|---|---|
| `react` + `react-dom` | The UI framework — lets you build with components |
| `react-router-dom` | Client-side routing (navigation without full page reloads) |
| `axios` | Makes HTTP requests to your backend API |
| `jwt-decode` | Decodes JWT tokens to read user info (name, role, etc.) |
| `framer-motion` | Smooth animations (fade-ins, slides, etc.) |
| `lucide-react` | Beautiful SVG icons as React components |
| `sockjs-client` + `@stomp/stompjs` | WebSocket libraries for real-time chat |

### [vite.config.js](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/vite.config.js)

Vite is your **build tool** — it bundles and serves your code during development. This config just enables two plugins: React support and Tailwind CSS.

### [tailwind.config.js](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/tailwind.config.js) & [index.css](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/index.css)

**Tailwind CSS** lets you style elements using utility classes directly in your HTML/JSX instead of writing separate CSS files. For example, `className="text-red-500 font-bold p-4"` means: red text, bold, padding of 1rem.

[index.css](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/index.css) imports Tailwind and sets up dark-mode support + base body styles.

