## 4. How the App Boots Up

### [main.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/main.jsx)

This is the **very first file that runs**. Here's what each line does:

```jsx
// 1. Import React and ReactDOM (the engine that renders to the browser)
import React from 'react'
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client'

// 2. Import your root component
import App from './App.jsx'

// 3. Import global styles
import './index.css'

// 4. Import context providers (explained in Section 6)
import { AuthProvider } from './context/AuthContext.jsx'
import { ThemeProvider } from './context/ThemeContext.jsx'

// 5. Find the <div id="root"> in index.html and mount React there
ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(
  <React.StrictMode>        {/* Development helper that warns about issues */}
    <AuthProvider>           {/* Makes login state available everywhere */}
      <ThemeProvider>        {/* Makes dark/light mode available everywhere */}
        <App />              {/* Your actual application */}
      </ThemeProvider>
    </AuthProvider>
  </React.StrictMode>,
)
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The **nesting order matters**. [AuthProvider](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/context/AuthContext.jsx#7-77) wraps [ThemeProvider](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/context/ThemeContext.jsx#5-39) which wraps [App](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/App.jsx#19-53). This means the entire app can access both auth and theme state. Think of it like Russian nesting dolls 🪆.

