## 5. The API Layer — axiosConfig.js

### [axiosConfig.js](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/api/axiosConfig.js)

This file creates a pre-configured HTTP client for talking to your Spring Boot backend:

```jsx
import axios from 'axios';

// Create an Axios "instance" with a base URL
// All requests will start with http://localhost:8080
const api = axios.create({
    baseURL: 'http://localhost:8080',
});

// INTERCEPTOR: Runs before EVERY request
// Automatically attaches the JWT token to the Authorization header
api.interceptors.request.use(
    (config) => {
        const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
        if (token) {
            config.headers['Authorization'] = `Bearer ${token}`;
        }
        return config;
    },
    (error) => Promise.reject(error)
);

export default api;
```

**Why this is smart:** Instead of manually adding the token to every API call, the interceptor does it automatically. Every file that imports `api` gets this behavior for free.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Component
    participant Axios Interceptor
    participant Backend

    Component->>Axios Interceptor: api.get('/api/v1/properties')
    Axios Interceptor->>Axios Interceptor: Read token from localStorage
    Axios Interceptor->>Backend: GET /api/v1/properties<br/>Authorization: Bearer <token>
    Backend-->>Component: JSON response
```

---

## 6. Context Providers (Global State)

### What is Context?

Normally, to share data between components you pass **props** from parent to child. But what if a deeply nested component needs the user's login status? You'd have to pass it through 5+ levels of components ("prop drilling"). **Context** solves this by making data globally accessible.

### [AuthContext.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/context/AuthContext.jsx)

This manages **everything about authentication**: login, register, logout, and knowing who the current user is.

**State variables:**

| Variable | Type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `user` | Object or null | `{ id, name, email, role }` — the logged-in user |
| `token` | String or null | The JWT token string |
| `isAuthenticated` | Boolean | `true` if the user is logged in |
| `loading` | Boolean | `true` while checking if a saved token is valid |

**Key functions:**

| Function | What it does |
|---|---|
| [login(email, password)](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/context/AuthContext.jsx#42-52) | POST to `/api/v1/auth/login`, saves the token |
| [register(name, email, password, role)](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/context/AuthContext.jsx#53-63) | POST to `/api/v1/auth/register`, saves the token |
| [logout()](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/context/AuthContext.jsx#64-70) | Clears the token, user, and localStorage |

**How token restoration works (the `useEffect`):**

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["App starts"] --> B{"Token in localStorage?"}
    B -- Yes --> C["Decode JWT with jwtDecode()"]
    C --> D{"Token expired?"}
    D -- Yes --> E["Call logout()"]
    D -- No --> F["Set user info from token<br/>(id, name, email, role)"]
    B -- No --> G["Set isAuthenticated = false"]
    F --> H["Set loading = false"]
    G --> H
    E --> H
```

**How any component uses it:**

```jsx
// In any component:
import { useAuth } from '../context/AuthContext';

const MyComponent = () => {
    const { user, isAuthenticated, login, logout } = useAuth();
    // Now you have access to everything!
};
```

### [ThemeContext.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/context/ThemeContext.jsx)

This manages **dark mode / light mode**. It:

1. Checks `localStorage` for a saved preference
2. Falls back to the OS system preference (`prefers-color-scheme: dark`)
3. Adds/removes the `dark` class on the `<html>` element (Tailwind uses this for dark mode styles)
4. Provides `isDarkMode` (boolean) and [toggleTheme()](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/context/ThemeContext.jsx#29-32) (function) to any component

