## 7. Routing & App.jsx

### [App.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/App.jsx)

This is the **heart of your app's navigation**. It uses React Router to decide which page to show based on the URL:

```jsx
<Router>                          {/* Enables client-side routing */}
  <Navbar />                      {/* Always visible on every page */}
  <Routes>
    <Route path="/" element={<Home />} />
    <Route path="/property/:id" element={<PropertyDetails />} />
    <Route path="/login" element={<Login />} />
    <Route path="/register" element={<Register />} />
    <Route path="/add-property" element={
      <PrivateRoute><AddProperty /></PrivateRoute>    {/* Login required */}
    } />
    <Route path="/dashboard" element={
      <PrivateRoute><Dashboard /></PrivateRoute>      {/* Login required */}
    } />
  </Routes>
</Router>
```

| URL | Page Shown | Auth Required? |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | Home | ❌ |
| `/property/5` | PropertyDetails (for property with id 5) | ❌ |
| `/login` | Login | ❌ |
| `/register` | Register | ❌ |
| `/add-property` | AddProperty | ✅ |
| `/dashboard` | Dashboard | ✅ |

### The [PrivateRoute](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/App.jsx#12-18) Component

```jsx
const PrivateRoute = ({ children }) => {
    const { isAuthenticated, loading } = useAuth();
    if (loading) return <LoadingSpinner />;
    return isAuthenticated ? children : <Navigate to="/login" />;
};
```

This is a **guard**. If you're not logged in and try to visit `/dashboard`, it automatically redirects you to `/login`. If you ARE logged in, it renders the child page normally.

