## 9. Pages — Deep Dive

### 🏠 [Home.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/pages/Home.jsx) — Property Listing

**What it does:** Fetches all properties from the backend and displays them in a searchable grid.

**React patterns used:**

| Pattern | Where | What's happening |
|---|---|---|
| `useState` | Lines 9-11 | Stores properties list, loading state, search term |
| `useEffect` | Lines 13-26 | Fetches properties from API **once** when component mounts (the `[]` dependency array means "run only once") |
| `.filter()` | Lines 28-31 | Client-side search filtering by title or address |
| `.map()` | Lines 74-120 | Renders a card for each property |
| Conditional rendering | Lines 66-122 | Shows "No properties found" or the grid |
| Framer Motion | Lines 75-80 | Staggered fade-in animation for each card |

**Data flow:**
```
Page loads → useEffect fires → api.get('/api/v1/properties')
→ setProperties(response.data) → React re-renders the grid
```

### 🔐 [Login.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/pages/Login.jsx) — Sign In Form

**What it does:** A form that collects email + password, calls [login()](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/context/AuthContext.jsx#42-52) from AuthContext.

**Key flow:**
```
User fills form → clicks Submit → handleSubmit() called
→ e.preventDefault() (stops page reload)
→ login(email, password) from AuthContext
→ If success: navigate('/') (go to Home)
→ If fail: setError(message) (show error)
```

**`e.preventDefault()`** — Without this, the browser would do a full page refresh when the form is submitted (old-school HTML behavior). In React, we prevent that and handle submission with JavaScript instead.

### 📝 [Register.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/pages/Register.jsx) — Sign Up Form

Very similar to Login, but with extra fields (name, role dropdown). Uses a single `formData` state object:

```jsx
const [formData, setFormData] = useState({
    name: '', email: '', password: '', role: 'ROLE_USER'
});

// One handler for ALL inputs (the `name` attribute matches the state key)
const handleChange = (e) => {
    setFormData({ ...formData, [e.target.name]: e.target.value });
};
```

> [!TIP]
> The `[e.target.name]` syntax is called a **computed property name**. If the input's `name="email"`, then `[e.target.name]` becomes `["email"]`, which updates just the `email` field. The `...formData` spread operator copies all existing values, so other fields aren't lost.

### ➕ [AddProperty.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/pages/AddProperty.jsx) — Create a Listing

**What it does:** A form to create a new property listing with an image upload and an AI description generator.

**Notable patterns:**

1. **Image upload with preview** (lines 29-39):
   ```jsx
   const reader = new FileReader();
   reader.onloadend = () => setImagePreview(reader.result);
   reader.readAsDataURL(file);
   ```
   `FileReader` converts the image file to a base64 string so you can show a preview *before* uploading.

2. **AI description generation** (lines 41-60):
   Calls `/api/v1/ai/generate` with the title+address as keywords, and auto-fills the description field.

3. **FormData for multipart upload** (lines 74-89):
   When sending both JSON and a file, you can't use regular JSON. Instead, you use the browser's `FormData` API to send a "multipart" request — the JSON goes as a `Blob` and the image goes as a file.

### 🔍 [PropertyDetails.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/pages/PropertyDetails.jsx) — View & Book a Property

The most complex page. It has **three major features**:

#### Feature 1: Property Display
Fetches a single property by ID from the URL (`useParams()`) and shows its details.

#### Feature 2: Real-Time Chat (WebSocket)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant React State
    participant STOMP Client
    participant Backend WebSocket

    User->>React State: Click "Chat" button
    React State->>Backend WebSocket: Load chat history (REST)
    React State->>STOMP Client: Connect via SockJS
    STOMP Client->>Backend WebSocket: SUBSCRIBE /topic/property/{id}
    
    User->>STOMP Client: Send message
    STOMP Client->>Backend WebSocket: PUBLISH /app/chat/{id}
    Backend WebSocket-->>STOMP Client: Broadcast message
    STOMP Client-->>React State: Add to messages array
    React State-->>User: Message appears in chat
```

- Uses **SockJS** (WebSocket fallback) + **STOMP** (messaging protocol on top of WebSocket)
- `useRef` stores the STOMP client so it persists across re-renders
- Another `useRef` + `useEffect` auto-scrolls to the latest message

#### Feature 3: Razorpay Payment
- Creates a payment order on the backend
- Opens the Razorpay checkout popup
- On success, creates a booking record

### 📊 [Dashboard.jsx](file:///c:/Users/akash/Desktop/smartlease/smartlease_frontend/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx) — User Profile & Management

**What it does:** Shows different content based on the user's role:

| Role | What they see |
|---|---|
| `ROLE_LANDLORD` / `ROLE_ADMIN` | Their listed properties + ability to delete them |
| `ROLE_USER` / `ROLE_TENANT` | Their bookings + links to view property details |

**Key pattern — role-based data fetching:**
```jsx
if (user?.role === 'ROLE_LANDLORD') {
    api.get('/api/v1/properties/my-properties');  // Fetch my listings
} else {
    api.get('/api/v1/bookings/my-bookings');       // Fetch my bookings
}
```

**Inline name editing** — The profile name can be edited in-place with a toggle between display and edit mode using `isEditingName` state.

