## 10. Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **SPA** | Single-Page Application — one HTML file, React swaps content dynamically |
| **Component** | A reusable piece of UI, written as a function returning JSX |
| **JSX** | HTML-like syntax inside JavaScript (compiled by Vite/Babel) |
| **Hook** | Special function (`useState`, `useEffect`, etc.) that adds features to components |
| **State** | Data that, when changed, causes the component to re-render |
| **Props** | Data passed from a parent component to a child component |
| **Context** | Global state accessible by any component without prop drilling |
| **Provider** | A component that wraps part of the tree to share context values |
| **Route** | A mapping from a URL path to a component |
| **Interceptor** | A function that runs before/after every HTTP request (Axios feature) |
| **JWT** | JSON Web Token — an encoded string containing user info + expiration |
| **WebSocket** | A persistent two-way connection for real-time communication |
| **STOMP** | Simple Text Oriented Messaging Protocol — used on top of WebSockets |
| **Tailwind CSS** | Utility-first CSS framework — style with class names like `text-red-500` |
| **Framer Motion** | Animation library for React — adds smooth transitions |
| **Vite** | Lightning-fast build tool and dev server for modern web apps |
